{
  "dom_id": "step-q280313",
  "name": "Question 8",
  "problem": "Which of the following is the graph of the polar curve $r=-7\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ?$",
  "worked_solution": "The polar equation $r=2a\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ defines a circle of radius $|a|$ centered at the point $(0,a).$\n\nIn our case, we have $r=-7\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,$ and therefore\n\n$$\na=\\frac{(-7)}{2}=-\\frac{7}{2}=-3.5.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation $r=-7\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ gives a circle of radius $|-3.5|=3.5$ centered at the point $(0,-3.5),$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14225098/assets/1ec8b2c39de3bbb0bf91cf5fd3c075e266e12c21b625171111576258825eeb48.png)",
